.TH SYSMONCTL 1 "2026" "sysmon 4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysmonctl \- query a running sysmond
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysmonctl
.RB [ \-s
.IR socket ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR seconds ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysmonctl
sends one command to
.BR sysmond (8)
over its unix socket and prints the reply. It exits with status 1 when
the daemon cannot be reached or answers with an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysmond (8)
